---
/** The seven layers, as in README.md "Why it is safe". Keep the two in step. */
---

<table class="layers">
	<caption>Each layer is enough on its own. All of them run together.</caption>
	<thead>
		<tr><th scope="col">Layer</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr>
	</thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr>
			<th scope="row">DB role</th>
			<td>
				<code>SELECT</code> on visible columns only. PII and secret columns are hidden at the
				Postgres level, so <code>SELECT *</code> on those tables fails. <code>default_transaction_read_only</code>, 10 s statement timeout, 1 s lock timeout,
				5 connections.
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<th scope="row">No stored password</th>
			<td>
				On AWS RDS the role logs in with a 15-minute IAM token minted from <em>your</em> AWS
				identity. Lose AWS access, lose Daypass access.
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<th scope="row">Real parser</th>
			<td>
				Every statement goes through Postgres's own parser (<code>libpg-query</code>). One
				statement; <code>SELECT</code> or <code>EXPLAIN</code> only; no <code>FOR UPDATE</code>, <code>SELECT INTO</code>, <code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code>, <code>pg_sleep</code>, <code>dblink</code>, <code>pg_read_file</code>, <code>set_config</code>, <code>nextval</code>, advisory locks, …
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<th scope="row">Result caps</th>
			<td>500 rows, 2 KB per cell, 1 MB per result. The model's context never floods.</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<th scope="row">Audit</th>
			<td>
				One JSON line per call in <code>~/.daypass/audit.jsonl</code>: time, caller (AWS ARN
				for IAM targets), lease id, reason, SQL, rows, ms, allowed/blocked.
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<th scope="row">Network</th>
			<td>
				Optional: punch your current IP into the DB security group for the lease, remove it on
				close or expiry.
			</td>
		</tr>
		<tr>
			<th scope="row">TLS</th>
			<td>Always verified. RDS targets pin the bundled AWS RDS CA.</td>
		</tr>
	</tbody>
</table>

<style>
	.layers {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 56rem;
		border-collapse: collapse;
		font-size: 0.925rem;
		line-height: 1.55;
	}
	caption {
		caption-side: top;
		text-align: left;
		color: var(--land-muted);
		padding-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	th,
	td {
		text-align: left;
		vertical-align: top;
		padding: 0.75rem 0.75rem 0.75rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline-light);
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}
	thead th {
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
		color: var(--land-muted);
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	tbody th {
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
		font-weight: 600;
		white-space: nowrap;
		width: 1%;
		padding-right: 1.25rem;
	}
	td:last-child {
		padding-right: 0;
	}
	@media (max-width: 30em) {
		tbody th {
			white-space: normal;
			min-width: 6rem;
		}
	}
</style>
